Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||07-30-2001||10:30 AM||||Now, I'm not going to be real thrilled to show up at fiero events to find more dark green cars... but hey- I love the color and you are certainly welcome to use it! =)<P>Anyway, my '87 GT was painted GM Medium Metallic Green (Courtsey of '95 Corvette and Cadillacs) and I had Gold Pearl custom mixed in to give it a better "sparkle" in the sunlight.  I also had my stock-gray '87 lace wheels refinished (PWS in Bloomington, MN)in a ford "honeywheat?" gold color... it's lighter than the stock '88 lace wheels.  The green and gold compliment perfectly with the tan interior...I love it! My only trouble is that I can't get a really good picture of the green/gold sparkle (the photo below was taken in the rain) and people think the car is black in the dark.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg"> <P>In this photo (taken at my wedding) you can see the green sparkle a little better in the background!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroWed.jpg"> <P>It's sunny today, so I might try to get a better photo on my digital camera...<P>Thanks!<BR>Rob Bartlett<BR>'87 GT Custom Green<BR>3.1L High-Output<BR>4spd OD tranny<BR>+Performance Mods!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cozmo||07-30-2001||10:40 AM||||Sean, you dog!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>That's the color combo I've decided to do my Targa in...<BR>I've seen a modern Mustang green that's very close to the color I want. I think it's a GREAT combination, kinda the British thing...<BR>I'm glad to see other green Fieros, yours looks good, Rob!<BR>It isn't easy being green...<BR><B>C02M0</B><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cozmosig.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000005||HummelHund||07-30-2001||12:17 PM||||From seeing these other cars now I know I want mine painted green! Now I wonder what minilite wheels would look like on a fiero...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I don't think any of you will have to worry about me being at shows anytime soon, my car's not exactly show quality...yet.<BR>By the way, Rob, that's a BEAUTIFUL car!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe, The "Black Wedge of Death" ($150 running car)||||reg||1
